  "decision": "Rejected and reverted. Borrowing file-owned type facts preserved exact semantics and reduced median wall time 1.671%, user CPU 1.797%, dependency readiness 1.074%, and semantic completion 1.080%, but it did not improve active-project readiness, slowed the live dependency probe 5.977%, and increased median peak RSS 4.091%. The ordinary release after revert is byte-identical to the accepted baseline. Do not repeat this broad borrowed iterator as an indexing optimization; profile a narrower store query keyed by subject and position, or target a distinct dominant path with an independently measurable budget win."
